What does this custom Agent check do each time it runs?
from datadog_checks.base import AgentCheck

class HelloCheck(AgentCheck):
    def check(self, instance):
        self.gauge('hello.world', 1, tags=['env:dev'])

Why do many custom checks start with this import?
try:
    from datadog_checks.base import AgentCheck
except ImportError:
    from checks import AgentCheck

flashcards.back:
from datadog_checks.base import AgentCheck
class HelloCheck(AgentCheck):
    def check(self, instance):
        self.gauge('hello.world', 1)
The class inherits AgentCheck; the Agent calls check() on every run.
